-- title:
--   Definitions of TypeDensity.Blowup.DivisorPoints
-- statement:
--   # Exceptional divisor points of two-chart curve data
--
--   For the blow-up of a regular local surface at its closed point, this file relates two-chart curve
--   data (finitely many points of the two charts with local curve generators) to divisors on the
--   exceptional line `ℙ¹_k`. It computes level-one kernels as products of powers of irreducible
--   polynomials, shows that a curve datum matching a divisor `Dv` has degree `deg Dv`, constructs curve
--   data realizing prescribed child ideals, and proves that the glued global function lies in the fixed
--   tangent cell.
--
--   ## Main results
--
--   * `TypeDensity.level_one_kernel_polynomial`: the level-one kernel on a blow-up chart maps to the
--     ideal of `k[X]` generated by a product of powers of distinct monic irreducibles;
--     `TypeDensity.two_chart_left_level_one_kernel_polynomial` specialises it to the left chart.
--   * `TypeDensity.child_ideals_curve_datum`: prescribed child ideals are realized by a curve datum.
--   * `TypeDensity.fixed_tangent_cell_curve_datum`: every ideal of the fixed tangent cell comes from
--     a curve datum matching `Dv`.
--   * `TypeDensity.matches_divisor_degree`: a curve datum matching `Dv` has degree `deg Dv`.
--   * `TypeDensity.matches_divisor_level_one_polynomial`: its level-one left kernel is generated by
--     the affine polynomial of `Dv`.
--   * `TypeDensity.global_function_has_tangent_divisor`, `TypeDensity.global_function_mem_cell`:
--     the glued global function has tangent divisor `Dv` and lies in the fixed tangent cell.
--
--   ## Implementation notes
--
--   Statements about the concrete surfaces `ConcreteSurface O pi u a b` are written with the local
--   notations `tChart`, `tExc`, ... for the blow-up charts and their data; see the notation section.
--
--   Provenance: `Thm_SurfaceBlowupV2_{boundary_contact_of_twisted_generator,
--   contracted_level_one_ideal_is_irreducible_power, two_chart_common_multiplicity_eq,
--   child_ideals_curve_datum, curve_datum_common_and_zero_clauses, curve_datum_matches_divisor,
--   matches_divisor_degree, fixed_tangent_cell_curve_datum, two_chart_left_level_one_kernel_polynomial,
--   matches_divisor_level_one_polynomial, global_function_has_tangent_divisor,
--   global_function_mem_cell}`.

